
Changes with AppServe 0.2.0                                      05 Oct 2026

    *) Change: Java, Node.js, and Perl application support and related
       packages and container images are removed.

    *) Change: listeners pass requests directly to fixed applications and
       targets; built-in routing, configuration variables, and NJS
       expressions are removed.

    *) Change: built-in TLS, static file serving, reverse proxying, upstream
       load balancing, and access logging are removed.

    *) Change: certificate and JavaScript module control APIs and the
       OpenSSL, PCRE, and NJS dependencies are removed.

    *) Feature: standard Forwarded header processing with listener
       forwarded.trusted IP/CIDR rules replaces legacy client_ip and
       X-Forwarded-* configuration.

    *) Change: unused job, cache, buffer filter, buffer pool, fiber, memory
       zone, vector, time parsing, and sendfile code is removed.


Changes with AppServe 0.1.0                                      05 Oct 2026

    *) Feature: initial AppServe release with runtime configuration and
       multi-language application hosting.

    *) Change: daemon, packages, services, default paths, and server
       identification use AppServe names; application API and binding
       identifiers are retained.
